# PandaCSS — Typography Utilities

| Key | Long form | Token |
|-----|-----------|-------|
| `fontFamily` | `font-family` | `fonts` |
| `fontSize` | `font-size` | `fontSizes` |
| `fontWeight` | `font-weight` | `fontWeights` |
| `lineHeight` | `line-height` | `lineHeights` |
| `letterSpacing` | `letter-spacing` | `letterSpacings` |
| `textAlign` | `text-align` | — |
| `textTransform` | `text-transform` | — |
| `textDecoration` | `text-decoration` | — (composite) |
| `textDecorationColor` | sub-prop | `colors` |
| `textOverflow` | `text-overflow` | — |
| `whiteSpace` | `white-space` | — |
| `wordBreak` | `word-break` | — |
| `textStyle` | shorthand → preset | `textStyles` |

## Prefer `textStyle` for typographic primitives

```tsx
<h1 className={css({ textStyle: "heading.h1" })}>Title</h1>
<p  className={css({ textStyle: "body.md" })}>Paragraph copy…</p>
```

Drop to per-property utilities only for **one-off** typographic adjustments:

```tsx
css({
  textStyle: "body.md",
  fontWeight: "medium",
  letterSpacing: "wide",
})
```

## Truncation pattern

```tsx
css({
  whiteSpace: "nowrap",
  overflow: "hidden",
  textOverflow: "ellipsis",
})
```

## Rules

- Establish typography via `textStyles` once; consume by name. Hand-set fontSize/lineHeight/weight at the call site only when overriding intentionally.
- `lineHeight` accepts unitless tokens (`1.1`, `1.5`) — those scale correctly with `fontSize` changes.
- `letterSpacing` tokens (`tight`, `normal`, `wide`) keep visual rhythm; don't sprinkle `em` values.
- For truncation in flex children, also set `minW: 0` on the child — otherwise `ellipsis` won't trigger.

